append.sd.path on | off\n\nON   put SD's program directory on your Windows PATH.\nOFF  take it off.\n\nWith no keyword it reports the current setting and changes nothing.\n\nThis is what lets "sd" run from any directory. It is your own PATH, not the\nmachine's, and the next install or upgrade puts it back. A terminal that is already\nopen keeps the PATH it started with; open a new one to see the change.
